# Copy to .env to point the app at a deployed API.
#
# Unset is the right setting for ordinary local work: src/lib/api.ts then uses
# the host Metro served the bundle from, on port 3000, which follows you onto a
# different network with no file to edit. Set this when the API is somewhere
# else — a dev deployment, or a physical device that cannot reach your laptop.
#
# App Runner serves HTTPS on 443, so there is no port and http:// will not work.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<id>.<region>.awsapprunner.com

# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is not a secret marker — anything with this prefix is inlined
# into the JavaScript bundle at bundle time and ships inside the app. Never put
# a credential here, and restart Metro with --clear after changing it, because
# the old value is baked into the cached bundle.
